[2026-11-10T10:58:53.868Z] [INFO]       "output": "After the uncommitted-changes restart budget is exhausted, auto-restart-until-mergeable still starts: second \"limit reached\" comment and the recovery commit is overwritten\n\n## What happens\n\nRun: `solve <issue-url> --model formal-ai --tool codex --attach-logs --verbose ...`, solve v2.39.10, 2026-11-10, pull request https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2. The provider is only the one used in the evidence run; the path below is taken by any tool or model whose sessions leave uncommitted changes until the restart budget is used up.\n\nTimeline (UTC, from the GitHub API unless a log line is given):\n\n| Time | Event |\n|---|---|\n| 09:22:43 | Restart 5/5 ends, the pull request is marked ready for review (log lines 2807-2810) |\n| 09:23:10 | Comment \"Auto-restart 5/5 Log\" with the last published log: https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2#issuecomment-6763709346 |\n| 09:23:18 | Recovery commit `cb00f1f5` (parent `693630a8`) pushed to `recovery/issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4` |\n| 09:23:20 | First comment \"Auto-restart 5/5 - limit reached\": https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2#issuecomment-6763712572 |\n| 09:23:23 | Pull request head becomes `8972c208` (the placeholder file is reverted) |\n| 09:25:36 | Second recovery commit `1319ca1e` (parent `8972c208`) pushed over the first one |\n| 09:25:38 | Second comment \"Auto-restart 5/5 - limit reached\": https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2#issuecomment-6763757247 |\n| 09:25:40 | The pull request is marked ready for review again; this is the final state |\n\nThe two comments differ in the blocker and in the commit:\n\n> **Remaining blocker:** uncommitted changes remained: M tests/verify-output.sh, ?? .github/\n> ... pushed to the branch `recovery/issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4` (commit cb00f1f5); the pull request branch was not changed.\n\n> **Remaining blocker:** The previous working session failed: auto-restart limit 5/5 reached; Uncommitted changes\n> ... pushed to the branch `recovery/issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4` (commit 1319ca1e); the pull request branch was not changed.\n\nSo the second \"limit reached\" names the first \"limit reached\" as its blocker.\n\nState left behind (checked 2026-11-10 after the run):\n\n- `recovery/issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4` points to `1319ca1e`. Commit `cb00f1f5`, which the first comment names, is no longer on any branch.\n- The recovery branch is 1 commit ahead of the pull request branch: `.github/workflows/main.yml` (+42) and `tests/verify-output.sh` (+38/-3). These are the changes the six sessions kept producing and never committed.\n- The pull request (head `8972c208`, 5 files) is open, ready for review, has 0 check runs, and does not contain the workflow file. On the recovery branch the workflow \"Run main.rs\" ran and succeeded (runs 42790298528 and 42790614141).\n- Nothing reads the recovery branch afterwards. Both comments end with \"Resolve the blocker, or rerun with a higher `--auto-restart-max-iterations`\" and give only the command that deletes the branch.\n- No log covers 09:22:51-09:25:40. The last published log ends at 09:22:51 (line 2837, start of its own upload), so the second exhaustion, the second push and the final ready flip are in no published log.\n\n## Expected\n\n- When a restart budget is exhausted the run ends: one \"limit reached\" comment, one recovery push, no second restart engine.\n- The preserved work is reachable: the comment says how to continue from it (for example the command that applies the recovery commit to the pull request branch), or the next `solve` run on the same pull request offers the recovery branch to the session.\n- The log of the final phase is published like every other phase.\n\n## Root cause\n\nCode read at 2.39.14 (commit b245deb62fbbca42625753587575416c50d81727). The evidence run is 2.39.10; whether the cited lines are identical in 2.39.10 was not verified. No log exists for the last 2.5 minutes, so the sequence below is derived from the code, the comment texts and the timestamps, not from a log.\n\n1. The watch loop exhausts the shared budget and calls `failOnAutoRestartBudgetExhausted` with `blocker: 'uncommitted changes remained: ...'` (`src/solve.watch.lib.mjs` lines 246-276). That keeps the pull request a deliberate draft (\"auto-restart limit 5/5 reached\"), pushes the recovery commit and posts the first comment ([`src/auto-restart-exhaustion.lib.mjs` lines 99-140](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/b245deb62fbbca42625753587575416c50d81727/src/auto-restart-exhaustion.lib.mjs#L99-L140)).\n2. `src/solve.mjs` then continues as after a normal watch run: line 1262 reverts the placeholder file, and [lines 1275-1286](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/b245deb62fbbca42625753587575416c50d81727/src/solve.mjs#L1275-L1286) start the second engine without looking at the watch result:\n\n   ```js\n   if (argv.autoMerge || argv.autoRestartUntilMergeable) {\n     const autoMergeResult = await startAutoRestartUntilMergeable({ ... });\n   ```\n\n   `auto-restart-until-mergeable` is on by default (`src/solve.config.lib.mjs` lines 308-312). `watchResult.autoRestartLimitReached` (`src/solve.watch.lib.mjs` lines 822-826) is not consulted.\n3. After its initial cooldown of 120 s (`src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs` lines 131 and 158; the gap between the two comments is 138 s) the second engine finds the deliberate failure draft and turns it into a restart reason, \"The previous working session failed: {{reason}}\" (`src/solve.auto-merge-guards.lib.mjs` lines 91-117, `locales/prompts/recovery.en.lino` line 26), then appends \"; Uncommitted changes\" (`src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs` lines 734-741). This is exactly the blocker text of the second comment.\n4. The budget is already exhausted, so `src/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs` lines 742-759 call `failOnAutoRestartBudgetExhausted` a second time. That function has no \"already reported\" guard, although its header says it posts a single comment. It commits the still uncommitted files again on the new head and force-pushes them over the first recovery commit (`src/critical-error-commit.lib.mjs` lines 99-163: `git push --force origin <commit>:refs/heads/recovery/<branch>`).\n5. At run end `restoreDeliberateDraftsAtRunEnd` (`src/pr-draft-state.lib.mjs` lines 206-233, hook in `src/solve.mjs` line 138) restores the pre-run state, which was \"ready\".\n\nThe recovery branch is written by `src/critical-error-commit.lib.mjs` and named in the comment (`describePreservedWork`, lines 77-84). A search of `src/` for a reader of `recovery/` branches found none; \"nothing reads it\" is based on that search.\n\nNot a defect, checked and dropped from this report: there is no \"Solution Draft Failed\" comment after \"limit reached\". That is intended; `src/tool-comments.lib.mjs` lines 272-297 treat the \"limit reached\" comment as the failure report.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- In `src/solve.mjs`, do not start `startAutoRestartUntilMergeable` when the watch run returned `autoRestartLimitReached` (or when `getAutoRestartLimitFailure()` is already set). Go straight to finalization.\n- Make `failOnAutoRestartBudgetExhausted` idempotent within a run: on a second call return the stored `limitFailure` without a new commit, push or comment.\n- Never overwrite an existing recovery commit with `--force`; if a second snapshot is really needed, build it on top of the first one or use a new branch name.\n- Put a way forward into the comment: the exact command that applies the recovery commit to the pull request branch, next to the command that deletes it. Optionally let the next run on the same pull request tell the session that `recovery/<branch>` exists.\n- Upload the log for the phase after the last restart (the upload at 09:22:51 is the last one in this run).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Comments: https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2#issuecomment-6763712572 and https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2#issuecomment-6763757247\n- Recovery branch: https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/tree/recovery/issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4 (compare with `issue-1-09b0c76bd0e4`: ahead 1, behind 0, 2 files)\n- Commits: https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/commit/cb00f1f5 and https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/commit/1319ca1e\n- Last published log (ends 09:22:51): https://gist.githubusercontent.com/konard/f0e689ac80237a960f865873b14f38b8/raw/1eae4c63babdd5783808d7c0f71330c3919dea2c/tmp-hive-mind-log-upload-usQxob-sanitized.log.txt, lines 2807-2810 and 2826-2837\n\n## Related issues\n\n- Related: #4031 (why the budget was used up in this run).\n- Related: #1355 (two restart engines; one engine would not hand an exhausted budget to the other; state: open).\n- Related: #3433 (recovery ignores git submodules; a different defect of the same recovery code; state: open).\n- Related: #2845 (item 2 there describes the \"stays a draft\" message followed by the run-end restore; state: open).\n- Related: #3434 (run-end restore marks a pull request ready after a failed run; state: open).\n\nReported from the analysis in https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1548.\n\n\n__formal_ai_exit=0\n",
